WEBVTT

00:00:03.710 --> 00:00:05.900
Dearest Mother in Heaven,

00:00:06.550 --> 00:00:10.030
The season of gloomy showers has arrived.

00:00:10.470 --> 00:00:14.220
Rain, rain, go away...

00:00:14.220 --> 00:00:15.780
Is it raining again, today?

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:18.620
It just keeps pouring down day in, day out...

00:00:19.790 --> 00:00:23.970
It's always rainy here when it gets round to June.

00:00:24.570 --> 00:00:27.850
Yeah, I guess it's the rainy season after all.

00:00:27.850 --> 00:00:30.280
It's not long until the pool reopens, though.

00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:32.970
As soon as the rain stops, it'll be summer vacation before you know it!

00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:34.780
Huh?

00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:36.890
Hey, wait...

00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:39.630
Something's not right here!

00:00:39.630 --> 00:00:40.930
But didn't we—!

00:01:05.990 --> 00:01:08.040
Kana... Your pendant...

00:01:09.700 --> 00:01:12.420
Thank you for faithfully watching up until now.

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:14.800
Look forward to Endoh's next project!{dongs}

00:01:42.790 --> 00:01:44.710
Didn't something like that happen?

00:01:44.710 --> 00:01:46.750
What are you talking about?

00:01:46.750 --> 00:01:48.210
It's still June.

00:01:48.530 --> 00:01:53.120
That might happen in the near future, but not just yet.

00:01:53.120 --> 00:01:55.270
In the near future?

00:01:55.270 --> 00:02:01.100
Yes. Why don't you look forward to that in about a month's time?

00:02:01.840 --> 00:02:02.720
Oh but...

00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:06.850
Miyamae, you need to stop getting ahead of yourself.

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:12.230
When God says it's June, it means it's June.

00:03:09.810 --> 00:03:11.140
I'm here too.

00:03:11.140 --> 00:03:14.270
Oh, never mind that! Kanako, swimming class starts today! {pool something class}

00:03:14.270 --> 00:03:18.730
School swimsuits! Butterfly stroke{hm, reference to stroke or beautiful girls/butterflies?}!
 And the forbidden mouth-to-mouth!

00:03:18.940 --> 00:03:20.190
There might even be... a{nipple} slip!

00:03:52.150 --> 00:03:54.690
Dearest Mother in Heaven,

00:03:54.690 --> 00:04:00.460
Due to a flood warning, the students of Ame-no-Kisaki have been confined to their dorms.

00:04:01.450 --> 00:04:06.450
The idiom "pouring buckets" really does seem quite suitable right now.

00:04:06.450 --> 00:04:11.080
Even if it wasn't forbidden, I wouldn't go out.

00:04:11.240 --> 00:04:13.080
Yeah, really.

00:04:13.330 --> 00:04:16.090
So, not that I'm complaining or anything...

00:04:18.970 --> 00:04:22.670
but why are we all cooped up in one room?

00:04:22.670 --> 00:04:28.930
So we could eat Shidoh's tasty snacks, of course.

00:04:28.930 --> 00:04:31.480
Such fabulous green tea could only come from Mt. Yame.

00:04:32.300 --> 00:04:37.370
Anyway, why do we need to have such eventful weather?

00:04:37.370 --> 00:04:43.530
Even these special boutique petit-fours{lit: high-quality http://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E7%B7%B4%E3%82%8A%E5%88%87%E3%82%8A} aren't enough to drive away the tedium.

00:04:44.840 --> 00:04:48.660
Dorm Mistress! I have just the thing to cheer you up!

00:04:51.340 --> 00:04:57.330
Why don't we play the Romance of the Three Kingdoms Generals card game that Paola Magnani from class 3-E created?{cluuuunk}{?}

00:04:58.710 --> 00:05:00.860
Romance of the Three Kingdoms... cards.

00:05:00.860 --> 00:05:05.590
Yeah. You're new to Ame-no-Kisaki, so you probably don't know.

00:05:05.590 --> 00:05:08.590
Paola's an exchange student from Italy.

00:05:08.590 --> 00:05:09.850
Italy?

00:05:10.230 --> 00:05:12.140
Italy, the land of passion?!

00:05:12.140 --> 00:05:14.090
What kind of beauty is she?!

00:05:14.090 --> 00:05:17.620
A classical beauty from Tuscany, built like a Roman statue?

00:05:17.620 --> 00:05:21.450
Or perhaps a shining beauty from Naples?

00:05:21.450 --> 00:05:25.200
Or maybe a spicy catch from Sicily?

00:05:25.200 --> 00:05:30.600
No matter what, if she's from the passionate land of Italy, she's got to be a real knockout!

00:05:31.970 --> 00:05:36.020
Why did I never realize there was such a beauty at my school?!

00:05:36.020 --> 00:05:38.580
Miyamae Kanako, epic fail...

00:05:40.090 --> 00:05:44.420
Paola's been a fellow Three Kingdoms friend of mine since before she came to Japan.

00:05:44.920 --> 00:05:49.680
The Internet really does make it easy to connect with those whom have common interests these days.

00:05:49.930 --> 00:05:51.730
Dear Mom above,

00:05:51.730 --> 00:05:54.460
This sounds like it's supposed to be a really touching story,

00:05:54.460 --> 00:05:57.560
but because it revolves around history nerds and the Three Kingdoms...

00:05:57.720 --> 00:06:00.310
It's really easy to play.{Sparkling}

00:06:00.670 --> 00:06:04.690
You just flip and match character description cards to their portrait cards!

00:06:05.360 --> 00:06:09.570
What do you do if you don't know a thing about the Three Kingdoms?

00:06:09.740 --> 00:06:11.590
No such person exists.

00:06:11.590 --> 00:06:12.850
Nope.

00:06:12.850 --> 00:06:14.200
Not one.

00:06:14.370 --> 00:06:15.790
What, impossible?!

00:06:16.120 --> 00:06:17.330
Even Yonakuni?!

00:06:17.610 --> 00:06:23.450
Before you get any wrong ideas, I don't have any particular fascination with the Three Kingdoms era.

00:06:23.450 --> 00:06:27.990
We just happen to be cultured, there's nothing more to it.

00:06:28.490 --> 00:06:30.840
Really? That's a relief.

00:06:32.840 --> 00:06:38.070
Kanako, if you could establish a kingdom and pick any ten generals as your followers, who would you choose?

00:06:38.070 --> 00:06:43.720
I'd pick Guo Jia, Xun Yu, Lu Su, Zhuge Liang, Mi Zhu, Lu Xun, Ma Chao...

00:06:43.720 --> 00:06:48.360
And maybe Zhang He, Cao Ren, and Taishi Ci to round things off, but I'm not too sure.

00:06:50.020 --> 00:06:51.820
She's for real!

00:06:53.490 --> 00:06:57.760
Geez, I don't really know much about history at all...{jeez works, too}

00:06:57.760 --> 00:06:59.990
Guo Jia? Really?

00:06:59.990 --> 00:07:05.190
Impertinent, but rather clever...

00:07:06.560 --> 00:07:11.100
That's right! Remember when his bad manners really set Chen Qun off?

00:07:11.610 --> 00:07:15.280
Guo Jia is definitely my favorite Wei general.

00:07:15.280 --> 00:07:18.020
Such a pity he died so young.

00:07:18.180 --> 00:07:23.810
It's like listening to the chatter of a bunch of old ladies who live near members of an idol group!

00:07:23.810 --> 00:07:26.900
Oh, Miyamae! Could you pass the dumplings?

00:07:28.160 --> 00:07:29.260
God.

00:07:29.260 --> 00:07:35.910
The Three Kingdoms were a long time ago. Why are you talking about it like it just happened yesterday?

00:07:36.490 --> 00:07:37.910
Hey, Ryuken!

00:07:37.910 --> 00:07:41.750
Let's stop worrying about the past and think about the future!

00:07:41.750 --> 00:07:42.960
What?!

00:07:44.340 --> 00:07:48.300
But...well, by studying our past, we can improve our future!

00:07:48.700 --> 00:07:49.460
So...

00:07:49.630 --> 00:07:52.340
But the people you're talking about are already dead!

00:07:52.500 --> 00:07:55.530
It'll never work! You'll always be yearning from afar!

00:07:55.530 --> 00:07:58.730
Plus, they all had loads of concubines anyway!

00:07:58.730 --> 00:08:00.800
That's why...

00:08:04.240 --> 00:08:06.000
I made her cry!

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:06.980
Oh man.

00:08:07.260 --> 00:08:13.360
I'm sorry, Kanako. I suggested this activity without taking your interests into consideration at all.

00:08:13.870 --> 00:08:15.740
That's right, Ishima.

00:08:15.740 --> 00:08:21.540
In this kind of situation, it's very important to consider what everyone else likes.

00:08:21.540 --> 00:08:25.650
And so I borrowed these from Tamaru in room 207!

00:08:25.650 --> 00:08:31.380
Look, it's Moe Concentration! Let's all play together!

00:08:31.620 --> 00:08:35.510
Just what kind of interests do you think I have, God?

00:08:36.850 --> 00:08:42.900
Now then, in Moe Concentration, you have to turn over two matching cards!

00:08:48.390 --> 00:08:53.370
They even have different-colored backs to help you tell them apart!

00:08:53.370 --> 00:08:58.840
So even a beginner can pick it up easily!

00:08:58.840 --> 00:09:01.830
I see! What a thoughtful game!

00:09:02.270 --> 00:09:03.540
Dorm mistress.

00:09:03.980 --> 00:09:06.870
If you'd like to play cards, I have these.

00:09:07.540 --> 00:09:11.680
Fun with Law: Criminal Law Set 2!

00:09:12.390 --> 00:09:15.000
Why does everyone have their own card game?

00:09:15.000 --> 00:09:20.120
These are the kind of thing someone like you who always lives on the edge should have.

00:09:20.120 --> 00:09:22.790
I don't always live on the edge! I live smack inside the safety zone!

00:09:22.790 --> 00:09:25.420
Don't slander me like that with no basis!

00:09:25.420 --> 00:09:29.180
Whether to avoid becoming the victim or the victimizer...

00:09:29.180 --> 00:09:32.440
everyone needs to know the law.

00:09:32.820 --> 00:09:39.450
Criminal Law Set 2 comes with a narrated CD requested by the fans of Set 1,

00:09:39.650 --> 00:09:42.990
so you can even play all by yourself!

00:09:43.450 --> 00:09:47.730
It was made to help out students in law school!

00:09:47.730 --> 00:09:49.500
Another thing made for yourself?!

00:09:49.500 --> 00:09:52.460
It's in its sixth printing.

00:09:52.460 --> 00:09:54.380
And people actually bought it?!

00:09:55.510 --> 00:10:02.260
The act of disturbing worship at shrines, temples, or graveyards...

00:10:03.100 --> 00:10:08.360
Section 188, the ban on slandering{blaspheming} places of worship and interference with services!{http://ja.wikibooks.org/wiki/%E5%88%91%E6%B3%95%E7%AC%AC188%E6%9D%A1}

00:10:09.050 --> 00:10:11.560
Matsurika, you don't have a set too, do you?

00:10:11.560 --> 00:10:12.880
I do.

00:10:12.880 --> 00:10:15.080
It's not particularly girly, but...

00:10:15.580 --> 00:10:18.320
I wonder what cards Matsurika has?

00:10:21.030 --> 00:10:24.660
This is nothing but a wishlist concealed as a card game!

00:10:25.140 --> 00:10:27.580
They're each labeled with their suggested retail price.

00:10:28.780 --> 00:10:33.000
Oh by the way, I removed the card for the diamond I received yesterday.

00:10:33.000 --> 00:10:36.590
You love shiny things, don't you?

00:10:37.960 --> 00:10:40.130
Et tu, Yonakuni?{LOL Shakespeare? Do geeks know Shakespeare? Had to look it up "Even you, namehere?"}

00:10:47.630 --> 00:10:52.130
Yonakuni's cards are like ESP cards.

00:10:54.110 --> 00:10:56.270
Why am I the only one without any cards?!

00:10:56.510 --> 00:10:59.860
I hate this! It sucks! I want my own cards too!

00:11:05.950 --> 00:11:07.380
Miyamae.

00:11:07.380 --> 00:11:10.960
If you wanted to have your own cards, why didn't you say so sooner?

00:11:11.760 --> 00:11:13.460
Father Kanae!

00:11:13.460 --> 00:11:15.930
You shouldn't be here, Father Kanae!

00:11:15.930 --> 00:11:18.620
This is the secret garden, the girls' dorm!

00:11:18.620 --> 00:11:23.050
No boys allowed, even if they are Ame-no-Kisaki teachers!

00:11:23.050 --> 00:11:26.800
Oh my, dorm mistress. Excuse me.

00:11:27.130 --> 00:11:31.330
The rain simply began pouring just when I happened to be in front of the Second Girls' Dorm.{derrrp this again}

00:11:31.330 --> 00:11:34.010
Ducking inside to avoid the deluge,

00:11:34.010 --> 00:11:39.230
My heart stirred when I heard Miyamae's cries for her own cards echoing from Shidoh's room.

00:11:39.230 --> 00:11:40.210
Oh...

00:11:40.210 --> 00:11:42.830
And I happened to bring this humble gift.

00:11:42.830 --> 00:11:46.700
One of the 50-inch 3D TVs that's been popular lately.

00:11:46.700 --> 00:11:48.450
Oh really?

00:11:48.710 --> 00:11:54.210
Well, there is a flood warning, so I guess you didn't have a choice.

00:11:54.210 --> 00:12:00.630
Yes. I certainly didn't come here to use Miyamae as an an excuse to check on Shidoh and Shinouji.

00:12:00.880 --> 00:12:02.220
Now, Miyamae.

00:12:02.370 --> 00:12:06.440
I, Kanae Toichirou, shall confide my own cards in you.

00:12:07.340 --> 00:12:09.850
Stay away! I'll break out!

00:12:10.350 --> 00:12:13.420
Shidoh! Shinouji! You two as well!

00:12:13.420 --> 00:12:15.300
I'll teach you all at once!

00:12:17.230 --> 00:12:20.110
Don't worry. The rules are simple.

00:12:20.360 --> 00:12:21.400
Now!

00:12:21.400 --> 00:12:22.390
Don't! Faargh!{to fit the next}

00:12:22.390 --> 00:12:27.320
A tonfa is a compact striking weapon developed in the Ryukyu Islands!

00:12:27.610 --> 00:12:28.580
Got it!

00:12:28.580 --> 00:12:30.180
I got it, Miyamae.

00:12:30.850 --> 00:12:32.460
Pilee polipee!{something that sounds like next line goes here}

00:12:32.460 --> 00:12:36.170
Filippo Lippi is a Renaissance artised based in Florence!

00:12:36.170 --> 00:12:37.130
There!

00:12:37.320 --> 00:12:38.640
What card game is this?

00:12:38.640 --> 00:12:42.200
Well, one about Kanako's screams of terror, I guess.

00:12:42.200 --> 00:12:46.350
Now then, what shall I have nex—

00:12:46.350 --> 00:12:48.760
Aww, the snacks are all gone?

00:12:48.960 --> 00:12:52.530
I should've prepared more. Oh well.

00:12:52.530 --> 00:12:55.520
Okay, since I have no more reason to be here,

00:12:55.520 --> 00:12:58.460
I think I'll make the rain go away now.

00:13:11.810 --> 00:13:15.820
Now then everyone, shall we go to lunch?

00:13:15.820 --> 00:13:19.540
Make sure you attend class in the afternoon.{edit}

00:13:21.450 --> 00:13:23.340
Mother up in Heaven,

00:13:23.340 --> 00:13:25.340
Well... Um...

00:13:25.340 --> 00:13:29.680
Oh, nothing. I don't care. It's fine!

00:13:35.280 --> 00:13:36.730
Mother up in Heaven,{COPSE or CORPSE?}

00:13:36.840 --> 00:13:39.340
Look at this beautiful blue sky.

00:13:39.650 --> 00:13:42.020
It's the perfect day for cleaning!

00:13:48.470 --> 00:13:49.480
Um...{matches sign - either set or sub should be skipped.}

00:13:49.610 --> 00:13:53.290
I'm terribly sorry to distract you two, but...

00:13:53.290 --> 00:13:55.160
If you're so sorry,

00:13:55.160 --> 00:13:57.290
then could you just not talk to us?

00:13:57.290 --> 00:13:59.560
Sure, as you wish.

00:14:08.340 --> 00:14:09.880
That's goddamn annoying!

00:14:11.050 --> 00:14:15.930
What's wrong with you?! I can't even enjoy a book on my precious Sunday off, with you doing that!

00:14:17.340 --> 00:14:18.700
What's <i>your</i> problem?!

00:14:18.700 --> 00:14:22.940
What are you doing, absorbed in a book or monster hunting again, while your roommate's stuck cleaning?!

00:14:22.940 --> 00:14:23.970
Help out!

00:14:23.970 --> 00:14:26.210
Who cares about your petty cleaning used to kill time.

00:14:26.210 --> 00:14:27.090
Petty cleaning?!

00:14:27.090 --> 00:14:30.530
This is a "team" battle. I'm in the middle of a tough fight right now.{like corporate receptions-matsurika is kissing ass by pting with w/e probably God}{I choose you, BROWN NOSE!}

00:14:30.970 --> 00:14:32.670
"Team"...battle?

00:14:33.260 --> 00:14:37.060
Where you have to avoid standing in front of them, stay out of their way, sucking up,

00:14:37.060 --> 00:14:44.000
support them without being noticed, clap, and say "nice shot" when they play well... That kind of "team" battle?

00:14:44.250 --> 00:14:48.290
If you understand, then keep quiet until I kill the dragon.

00:14:48.290 --> 00:14:51.510
The future of the Second Girls' Dorm rests upon this battle.

00:14:52.680 --> 00:14:54.630
I see.

00:14:54.630 --> 00:14:58.300
I won't even embarrass myself by asking who you're "teaming" up with.

00:14:59.210 --> 00:15:00.340
I pray for your victory.

00:15:00.340 --> 00:15:02.190
Prayer received.

00:15:06.520 --> 00:15:11.750
Reception is difficult, but it's nice having servant animals.

00:15:12.110 --> 00:15:15.580
I'm getting some gloomy vibes from you, Matsurika.

00:15:15.860 --> 00:15:18.870
Some people like dogs or cats. I like slaves.

00:15:19.030 --> 00:15:20.680
Your point?

00:15:21.660 --> 00:15:24.820
What did you need, anyway, Kanako?

00:15:24.820 --> 00:15:26.170
Oh, right!

00:15:26.170 --> 00:15:29.950
I'm telling you, if you don't pay attention to cleaning, places like this—

00:15:32.160 --> 00:15:33.550
Wait, what?

00:15:33.730 --> 00:15:34.990
There's no dust!

00:15:34.990 --> 00:15:37.560
Hey, don't get your skin oils all over it!

00:15:41.320 --> 00:15:46.610
I never noticed it before, but doesn't Mariya's living space shine so brightly?!

00:15:46.610 --> 00:15:48.320
And what could this scent be?

00:15:48.320 --> 00:15:50.440
Rose, jasmine, neroli...

00:15:50.440 --> 00:15:54.190
The sweetness of so many flowers, with the refreshing hint of bergamot and orange...

00:15:54.190 --> 00:15:56.550
What a fresh fragrance!

00:15:56.550 --> 00:16:00.250
My desecrate body doesn't even deserve the slightest caress of this divinity, much less be enveloped in it!

00:16:00.530 --> 00:16:02.750
Such purity! Such divinity!

00:16:03.810 --> 00:16:05.500
This is the First World!{what.}{praising the country's advances in fragrance technology?}

00:16:05.500 --> 00:16:08.670
I'd like to develop my Third World tracts of land!

00:16:08.670 --> 00:16:11.130
Please give me some Overseas Development Aid!{oh now i get it it's a huge foreign aid metaphor}

00:16:11.250 --> 00:16:12.250
Rejected.

00:16:12.250 --> 00:16:13.520
Subprime!

00:16:13.520 --> 00:16:14.720
You moron!

00:16:14.720 --> 00:16:17.930
Why do you need aid and technical support?!

00:16:17.930 --> 00:16:24.310
Half shines bright, and half is dim! We attend the same school and live in the same room, so why do these gaps open up?!

00:16:24.590 --> 00:16:28.500
Now is the time to sound the alarm on our twisted society!

00:16:28.500 --> 00:16:29.980
What are you blogging about?!

00:16:31.400 --> 00:16:35.490
I want a maid to clean for me too!

00:16:36.630 --> 00:16:39.440
That's it! If I had my own lovable little maid...

00:16:39.440 --> 00:16:43.310
Not only could she clean for me, I could put my head on her lap, have her clean my ears,{Houki}

00:16:43.310 --> 00:16:47.690
have her read to me, and do this and that...{Cecilia/Chinagirl}

00:16:47.690 --> 00:16:50.020
And oooh, maybe even <i>that...{HANAZAWAWAWAWAWAWA/MatsurikaLoli}</i>

00:16:51.090 --> 00:16:54.090
You just cleaned! Why are you making another mess?

00:16:54.090 --> 00:16:55.440
You're a meanie, Mariya!

00:16:55.440 --> 00:16:59.550
You too, Matsurika! With your touching and your stripping and all that!

00:16:59.550 --> 00:17:00.720
Wait, what stripping?

00:17:00.940 --> 00:17:06.310
My gosh. Basically you just want someone to help you with your cleaning, right?

00:17:07.530 --> 00:17:10.150
I've already arranged for that.

00:17:15.240 --> 00:17:16.240
Miyamae.

00:17:16.500 --> 00:17:21.240
You should've told me you were too weak to do your own cleaning.

00:17:21.810 --> 00:17:25.320
I only managed to come today because Shido sent me a text...

00:17:26.380 --> 00:17:28.460
What's wrong, Miyamae?!

00:17:28.460 --> 00:17:31.540
She's foaming at the mouth! Someone! Call an ambulance!{911 localised to US, 000 for Aus, 119 for Japan, 999 for Hong Kong, just call it ambulance for everyone i guess}

00:17:31.540 --> 00:17:35.840
Now, now, Kanako. You shouldn't overdo things, weak as you are.

00:17:36.180 --> 00:17:37.470
Mother in Heaven,{but it's after dawn}{don't know if capitalize?}

00:17:37.780 --> 00:17:40.470
Cleaning is something one must do for oneself.

00:17:40.470 --> 00:17:44.060
One must live befitting one's stature.

00:17:49.480 --> 00:17:52.860
Did you notice? I bought new glasses.

00:17:55.560 --> 00:17:58.490
I can't ask "notice what?" now, can I...?

00:17:58.490 --> 00:18:01.120
I don't think they're any different than before...

00:18:01.620 --> 00:18:04.160
but I'll just have to fake it for now!

00:18:05.070 --> 00:18:06.870
They have a different shine to them!

00:18:06.870 --> 00:18:11.150
Yeah, they do! Your new lenses have a different shine!

00:18:11.150 --> 00:18:13.030
Your lenses?! That's what it was?!

00:18:13.030 --> 00:18:16.270
You replaced your old plastic ones with glass, didn't you?

00:18:16.270 --> 00:18:18.260
They look good on you, Kiri.

00:18:18.260 --> 00:18:22.430
Yeah, my old ones were all scratched up...

00:18:22.860 --> 00:18:27.770
so I rewarded myself for doing well on my midterms by buying these.

00:18:29.360 --> 00:18:33.090
What were you thinking rewarding yourself with new lenses?

00:18:33.090 --> 00:18:35.860
Why didn't you get something cuter?

00:18:35.860 --> 00:18:39.740
Actually, I gave myself a reward for improving my grades too!

00:18:42.080 --> 00:18:45.120
The tri-wing screwdriver I've always wanted!

00:18:45.120 --> 00:18:47.950
That isn't cute either!

00:18:48.400 --> 00:18:50.830
What the heck is a tri-wing screwdriver, anyway?

00:18:51.150 --> 00:18:53.800
The tri-wing screwdriver;

00:18:53.800 --> 00:18:59.090
a special tool used for devices that the manufacturer doesn't want the end user to take apart.

00:18:59.480 --> 00:19:03.070
Next time I'm gonna aim for a security Torx!

00:19:03.070 --> 00:19:05.350
What a wonderful reward, Momoi.

00:19:05.350 --> 00:19:11.500
I'm kind of curious why you two care so much about different screwdrivers...

00:19:11.910 --> 00:19:16.250
What exactly are you going to take apart with that, Sachi?

00:19:16.250 --> 00:19:18.480
I don't have anything in mind yet.

00:19:18.720 --> 00:19:22.320
I just want to have anything, anywhere.

00:19:23.480 --> 00:19:25.450
She's preparing to be helpful...{lit. "she endeavored"}

00:19:25.700 --> 00:19:28.670
I guess it's nice to reward yourself.

00:19:29.150 --> 00:19:31.780
Did you get something too, Yuzuru?

00:19:33.470 --> 00:19:35.370
You're terrible, Kanako!

00:19:35.710 --> 00:19:38.340
You're just trying to embarrass me!

00:19:39.230 --> 00:19:40.340
Why are you crying?!

00:19:41.670 --> 00:19:45.030
I'm sorry I bought myself a whole bunch of my favorite chocolates!

00:19:45.030 --> 00:19:49.430
I'm so sorry it's not anything interesting like Sachi or Kiri got!

00:19:49.430 --> 00:19:52.020
Don't worry, Yuzuru.

00:19:52.020 --> 00:19:55.240
This isn't some kind of reflection on your personality.

00:19:55.240 --> 00:19:59.030
If anything, sweets are a little cute. I like it!

00:20:00.310 --> 00:20:03.200
And wow, these chocolates are really expensive!

00:20:04.250 --> 00:20:05.820
They're not "a little" anything!

00:20:06.200 --> 00:20:10.540
I ate them one by one, treasuring each one like gems...I'm so sorry!

00:20:10.870 --> 00:20:12.840
Chocolates as gems, huh?

00:20:12.840 --> 00:20:18.290
What a completely different meaning compared to Matsurika's wish list...

00:20:18.290 --> 00:20:20.380
Yuzuru is cute.

00:20:20.900 --> 00:20:23.510
So that's what we talked about today.

00:20:23.740 --> 00:20:27.380
I want something too, Mariya.

00:20:27.380 --> 00:20:31.390
What do I look like, a certain blue and white cat-robot with a fourth-dimensional pouch?{lit tanuki-looking but a western audience probably needs to doraemon ref shoved in their faces}{alternative could be genie, or perhaps an even more obscure reference to Laputa and Pazu's 'magical' bag}

00:20:31.390 --> 00:20:33.640
I want a reward, Mariemon!

00:20:35.290 --> 00:20:41.920
Rewards are usually reserved for those who work hard, and then given when they succeed.

00:20:41.920 --> 00:20:43.650
What have you done?

00:20:44.010 --> 00:20:45.910
Shamefully, not a thing{Not a thing}!

00:20:47.340 --> 00:20:48.410
I know.

00:20:48.740 --> 00:20:53.140
Yes, I know I'm a useless do-nothing loser.

00:20:53.690 --> 00:21:02.730
But imagine! Within me could be an unknown spiritual shine I could use to communicate with you all!

00:21:03.370 --> 00:21:05.840
Take heed, Mariya, Matsurika!

00:21:05.840 --> 00:21:08.390
Consider my latent potential to try hard!

00:21:09.390 --> 00:21:11.010
You're terrible, Mariemon!

00:21:12.640 --> 00:21:15.370
I want a reward too!

00:21:15.370 --> 00:21:16.390
Very well.

00:21:21.480 --> 00:21:22.730
Miyamae.

00:21:22.730 --> 00:21:27.740
If you were concerned that you weren't trying hard enough, you should have just sought my counsel.

00:21:28.310 --> 00:21:34.000
Of course, I didn't just come here using you as a pretext to get at Shidoh and Shinouji,{thidn't or didn't?}

00:21:34.000 --> 00:21:37.460
What's wrong?! Miyamae is foaming at the mouth again!

00:21:37.460 --> 00:21:39.460
Someone! Call an ambulance!

00:21:39.460 --> 00:21:43.130
Oh my. Kanako, you must be working yourself too hard.

00:21:43.350 --> 00:21:44.760
Mother in Heaven...

00:21:44.910 --> 00:21:48.900
Surely you can see how hard I'm working, can't you?

00:21:48.900 --> 00:21:53.370
A reward of setting me free from these circumstances would satisfy me!

00:23:28.390 --> 00:23:33.720
{salutation-dropped}As the blue sky peeks through the clouds and summer approaches,

00:23:33.720 --> 00:23:36.700
beloved mother in Heaven, how do you fare?

00:23:37.020 --> 00:23:41.330
Recently my student, Shidoh Mariya, has been texting me regularly.

00:23:41.670 --> 00:23:45.430
I'm not sure how to respond properly.

00:23:45.430 --> 00:23:48.350
Well, not unsure about the content of the response.

00:23:48.350 --> 00:23:51.470
I'm unsure of whether or not to use a emoticon.

00:23:51.760 --> 00:23:55.780
A text is nothing more than a short message, is it not?

00:23:55.780 --> 00:24:00.390
If I don't convey my message properly, there's great potential for the wrong impression to be made.

00:24:00.850 --> 00:24:07.060
At times like these, if I use a grinning smilie or something, I should be able to avoid any unwanted misunderstandings.

00:24:07.700 --> 00:24:10.900
But I am a teacher of the Japanese language.

00:24:10.900 --> 00:24:15.070
Thus, is it proper for me to rely on a simple emoticon?

00:24:15.070 --> 00:24:21.080
Shall I take on the challenge of using proper Japanese to express my feelings?

00:24:21.810 --> 00:24:27.510
No, but it's been said that modern schoolgirls simply ignore excessively long texts.

00:24:28.300 --> 00:24:30.170
Ergo, that option is closed.

00:24:31.300 --> 00:24:37.180
But amongst the sea of emoticons, which one should I choose?

00:24:38.160 --> 00:24:40.720
This one? Maybe this one? Or this one?

00:24:40.720 --> 00:24:42.980
No, maybe this one!

00:24:44.060 --> 00:24:45.050
This one!

00:24:45.050 --> 00:24:49.110
If I use this adorable little chick—!

00:24:49.110 --> 00:24:50.110
Do our best, Toichiro!

00:24:50.790 --> 00:24:54.430
Ikkyu, can you bind mai waifu in red rope for me?

00:24:54.660 --> 00:24:59.180
First bring your 2D waifu out of the screen, shogun.

00:24:59.480 --> 00:25:02.600
Thus that summer, the shogun becomes aquainted with image editing.

00:25:02.940 --> 00:25:05.070
The Photoshop shogun.
